---
// VISUAILS — Cookie Policy. Ported verbatim from the SvelteKit
// cookie-policy page (itself ported verbatim from static
// /cookie-policy.html). Legal pages are deliberately plain/scannable,
// not "designed" — no reveal animations or kickers, per the rebuild
// brief. Body copy is untouched — only the wrapper markup is adapted to
// Astro/Layout conventions.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy — VISUAILS"
  description="How VISUAILS uses cookies: essential cookies by default, analytics only with your consent."
>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow-page">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size:var(--t-page-h1)">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p style="margin-top:.8rem;color:var(--ink-3)">Last updated: August 2026</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section-tight"><div class="container narrow legal stack-lg">
    <div><h2>What cookies are</h2><p style="margin-top:.6rem">Cookies are small text files a website can store on your device. They're commonly used to make sites work, remember preferences, and measure how a site is used.</p></div>
    <div><h2>How we use them</h2><p style="margin-top:.6rem">The VISUAILS website is largely static. By default we only use <strong>essential</strong> cookies needed for the site to function and to remember your privacy choices. We do not load advertising or tracking cookies without your consent.</p>
    <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong>Essential</strong> — basic functionality and security. Always on.</span></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong>Analytics</strong> — anonymous usage measurement. Only with your consent.</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    <div><h2>What we actually set today</h2><p style="margin-top:.6rem">Naming them is more useful than describing categories, so here they are in full. This is the complete list.</p>
    <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong><code>vis_account</code></strong> — keeps you signed in to VISUAILS Studio after you click the sign-in link in your email. Essential. Expires after 30 days, or when you sign out.</span></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong><code>vis_admin</code></strong> — the admin side login. Essential. Never set on a visitor's device.</span></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong><code>vis_consent</code></strong> — remembers the choice you made in the cookie banner, so we stop asking. Essential, and the reason a refusal sticks. Expires after 12 months, when we ask again.</span></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong><code>vis_lang</code></strong> — remembers whether you read VISUAILS Studio in Dutch or English, set only when you use the language switch there. Essential. Expires after 12 months.</span></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span><strong><code>vis_nav</code></strong> — remembers whether you collapsed the menu in VISUAILS Studio, set only when you click that button. Essential. Expires after 12 months.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem">That is all five. No advertising cookies, no tracking pixels, no third-party embeds, and no analytics unless you switch it on — at which point it is Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is itself cookieless and sets nothing on your device. We share nothing with anyone.</p></div>
    <div><h2>Managing cookies</h2><p style="margin-top:.6rem">Use the <button type="button" class="legal-cc" data-cc-reopen>cookie preferences</button> link — it is in the footer of every page — to change your answer at any time, including withdrawing a yes. Refusing is exactly as easy as accepting and costs you nothing: the site works identically either way. You can also clear or block cookies in your browser settings, though blocking the essential ones will stop the client portal remembering you.</p></div>
    <div><h2>Contact</h2><p style="margin-top:.6rem">Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@visuails.com">hello@visuails.com</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Legal-text typography — page-scoped, plain and scannable by design. */
  .narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  .stack-lg { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2.2rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.7; }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent-bright); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  /* The withdrawal control inside body copy. It is a <button> because it opens
     a panel, and it is styled as the link beside it because a button that
     looks like a button in the middle of a sentence reads as an advert. */
  .legal-cc { background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; color: var(--fill-blue); cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal-note { padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
</style>
